  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 208 PM CDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nCurrently, broad ridging extends across the central portions of the \ncountry. A weak shortwave trough is situated over the Central \nRockies and will continue to traverse the Central Plains through the \nrest of today and into early Wednesday. This feature is leading to \nscattered cloud cover along with passing showers/sprinkles. \nTemperatures are only being impacted directly underneath \nprecipitation and highs across the area will generally top out in \nthe lower 70s this afternoon. Lows tonight will remain mild with \ntemperatures only falling into the middle 50s areawide. A few \nshowers and sprinkles will continue to dot the forecast area through \nWednesday morning with no appreciative rainfall expected with any of \nthis activity.\n\nThrough the end of the week, a narrow yet stout ridge will be \ncentered over the Plains leading to continued above normal \ntemperatures. Afternoon highs each day will reach into the middle to \nupper 70s through Saturday with overnight lows generally falling \ninto the 50s. Dry conditions with minimal cloud cover are \nanticipated through Friday.\n\nTroughing will move over the western U.S. by Friday with a \ncorresponding surface low deepening over the Northern Rockies. This \nfeature will lead to a tightening pressure gradient over the Central \nPlains on Friday and increasing southerly winds. Precip chances will \nbegin increasing for western Kansas on Saturday as the upper level \ntrough and surface front slowly nudge eastward. By Sunday and into \nMonday, this system will pass over the region bringing increasing \nprecipitation chances areawide along with cooler temperatures.",
